> for m.new is a huge matrix(14,295,768 x 6). When proccessing the last row
> of code, I receive:
> 
> Unable to obtain requested dynamic memory.
> 
> What way could I solve this problem?

It is likely that you are really out of memory. m.new is about 650Mb
(if the contents are real numbers), and you need two copies at least
(the old one and the new one). (I am suprised you got this far.) It is
hard to know without trying it what might use a little less memory,
but

m.new <- cbind(xlocs[i],ylocs[i],slocnum[i],xloct[i],yloct[i],tlocnum[i])

might work.  I suspect you will find it difficult to do much else
with this matrix, and it might well be better to work with the columns
separately.

