From fharrell at virginia.edu  Tue Apr 18 15:23:45 2000
From: fharrell at virginia.edu (Frank E Harrell Jr)
Date: Tue, 18 Apr 2000 11:23:45 -0400
Subject: [S] Additions to S+ Hmisc Library
Message-ID: <38FC7E01.CFB9DE0E@virginia.edu>

New functions have been recently added to Hmisc:

- event.chart - a function by Lee, Hess, Dubin (American Statistician Feb
2000) - draws very
      flexible event charts; added to Hmisc with kind permission of the
authors
- plotDraw - a function for interactively drawing and saving points and
curves for teaching, e.g.
     drawPlot(Points('Males'), Points('Female'), Curve('Fitted'))
- putKey, putKeyEmpty - help in using key().  putKeyEmpty puts a key in the
most empty
     region of a plot, given the coordinates of all points yet drawn
- latex.* - the family of functions used to typeset many types of S+
objects in LaTeX, from
     the print.display library of Rich Heiberger and myself; includes
utility functions format.df and
     latex.translate

xYplot, the enhanced version of xyplot, has been further enhanced to allow
the user
to specify a function for aggregating data before plotting, when drawing
lines and
error bars or bands.

Problems have been corrected in areg.boot, sas.get, transcan, and somers2.

The document An Introduction to S-Plus and the Hmisc and Design Libraries
by
Alzola and Harrell has been updated.  This is the main document upon which
the
upcoming MathSoft course "S-Plus for Statistical Data Analysis and
Graphics" is based
(May 8-9, Washington DC).

S-Plus users may obtain Hmisc for Windows/NT/Unix from
http://hesweb1.med.virginia.edu/biostat/s/Hmisc.html
Statlib's version is out of date due to problems with our ftp server which
will be fixed soon.

